---
description: Apply when producing a table, dataset, count, or total from a source.
alwaysApply: false
---

# Data provenance

- When producing tables or datasets, record for each value where it came from. Mark anything not directly read from a source.
- Report counts and totals computed from the data, not from memory of the data.
- Never fill in, estimate, or interpolate a value without saying so, and never when a real source is accessible.
- If an approximation is the only option, ask the user first and mark every affected value.
